A directive on the losing declaration of a redeclared name: go/types gives the second
declaration no object, so without a check the directive would silently vanish while the
rest of the set generates: exit 0, provider gone, its type quietly an injector input.
The loader reports the redeclaration itself as a tolerated type error; the directive
still fails loudly.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrInvalidType
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type Config struct{}

//plumb:build
func NewConfig() *Config { return &Config{} }

func F() {}

//plumb:build
func F() *Config { return nil }
